b = 7  # Length of the other parallel side
h = 4  # Height of the trapezoid

# Calculate the area
area = calculate_area(a, b, h)
print("Area of the trapezoid:", area)
```

### Symmetries and Rotational Invariance
- A trapezoid does not have rotational symmetry of order 4 like a square. However, an isosceles trapezoid (where the non-parallel sides are equal) has a line of symmetry that bisects the two non-parallel sides.
- It has rotational symmetry of order 2 (180 degrees) if it is isosceles.

