### Step 1: Define the Variables
- Principal (P) = $1,000
- Annual interest rate (r) = 5% = 0.05
- Inflation rate (i) = 2% = 0.02
- Number of compounding periods per year (n) = 4 (quarterly)
- Time in years (t) = 10

### Step 2: Calculate the Effective Interest Rate
The effective interest rate after adjusting for inflation is:
\[
\text{Effective Rate} = r - i = 0.05 - 0.02 = 0.03
\]

### Step 3: Apply the Compound Interest Formula
The formula for compound interest is:
\[
A = P \times \left(1 + \frac{r - i}{n}\right)^{n \times t}
\]
Substituting the values:
\[
A = 1000 \times \left(1 + \frac{0.03}{4}\right)^{4 \times 10}
\]
\[
A = 1000 \times \left(1 + 0.0075\right)^{40}
\]
\[
A = 1000 \times (1.0075)^{40}
\]

