A real-world scenario where robust statistics are preferred is in financial analysis. Financial data often includes extreme values (e.g., stock prices during a market crash), which can significantly distort traditional statistical measures. Using robust statistics helps in identifying trends and patterns that are not unduly influenced by these outliers, leading to more accurate financial modeling and forecasting.

